      "citation": "Gansevoort RT, et al. (CKD Prognosis Consortium). Lower estimated GFR and higher albuminuria are associated with adverse kidney outcomes: a collaborative meta-analysis. Kidney Int. 2011;80(1):93-104",
      "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21289597/",
      "notes": "CKD-PC ESRD-specific HRs are far steeper (eGFR 45 -> ~29, 15 -> ~454 vs eGFR 95). Values here are deliberately attenuated because the modeled outcome is broader CKD progression, not ESRD alone."
    },
